rem Digital Root Sums of Factorisations
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=159
rem Sum the maximal digital root sums of
rem the factorisations of every n from 2
rem to Limit - 1

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 1000000

rem Best[m] is the larger of dr(m) and
rem dr(d) + Best[k] over m = k d. Here
rem Best[k] is final once all k up to
rem k / 2 are done, so the ks of a block
rem [B, 2 B) are settled together and
rem each d pushes its products at once.
rem Below the root go one k at a time.
N = 0 till Limit array
Dr = (N - 1) mod 9 + 1
Dr 0 = 0
Best = Dr copy
Root = Limit isqrt
for K in 2 to Root - 1
  Top = (Limit - 1) // K
  Slot' = K * 2 to K * Top by K
  New = (Dr (2 to Top)) + Best K
  Best Slot = (Best Slot) max New
end
B = Root
for B at most Limit // 2
  Ks' = B to 2 * B - 1 array
  Mine = Best Ks copy
  for D in 2 to (Limit - 1) // B
    Reach = (Limit - 1) // D
    Hi = (2 * B - 1) min Reach
    Cut = Hi - B + 1
    Slot' = B * D to Hi * D by D
    New = (Mine take Cut) + Dr D
    Best Slot = (Best Slot) max New
  end
  B = B * 2
end
Rest = Best drop 2
Answer = Rest sum
Answer print
